.TH OOB 1 "March 2026" "apt-oob 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oob \- out-of-band software manager for Debian-based systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oob
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oob
manages software that has no apt repository \(em packages distributed as
tarballs with a download URL \(em handling version checking, verification,
installation, and symlinking.
.PP
It integrates with the standard apt upgrade process via a DPkg::Post\-Invoke
hook and runs automatically after
.BR apt\ upgrade (8)
or
.BR apt\-get\ upgrade (8).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI update " [name]"
Check available versions without downloading or installing.
Prints installed and available versions for each package.
.TP
.B upgrade
Download and install all available updates for enabled packages.
Downloads the archive to a temporary directory, verifies checksum and
signature if configured, removes the old install directory, extracts,
creates symlinks, and writes the state file. A verification summary line
is printed after checks complete (e.g. "gpg OK  checksum OK"). If
extracted files have restrictive permissions, they are fixed automatically.
Per-package failures are logged and skipped; remaining packages still
get a chance to update.
.TP
.BI install " name"
Install or update a single package by
.IR name .
.TP
.BI remove " name"
Remove installed files from
.IR live/ ,
symlinks, and the state file for a package. Also disables the package
config (renames to .disabled) to prevent reinstallation on next upgrade.
Prompts y/n before proceeding unless
.B \-\-force
is specified.
.TP
.B list
List all configured packages and their installed versions.
Packages with a conf.d entry but no state file are shown as
"configured, not installed". Disabled packages are shown as "disabled".
.TP
.BI status " [name]"
With no arguments, show a system-wide health summary including apt hook
status, enabled/disabled package counts, update availability, and symlink
health. With a package
.IR name ,
show the state file contents for that package and run the version check
script to report whether an update is available.
.TP
.BI enable " name"
Enable a disabled package by renaming its config from .disabled back
to the original name.
.TP
.BI disable " name"
Disable a package by appending .disabled to its config filename.
Disabled packages are skipped by
.B upgrade
and
.BR update .
.TP
.B init
Create the directory structure under
.IR OOB_BASE ,
copy the
.B oob
binary into
.IR bin/ ,
write a default
.I /etc/apt\-oob.conf
if it does not exist, write example package configs if
.I conf.d/
is empty, and install the apt post\-invoke hook at
.IR /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99\-apt\-oob .
Warns and prompts if the hook already exists.
.TP
.B deinit
Remove the apt post\-invoke hook file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
For
.BR install / upgrade :
re-download and reinstall regardless of installed version.
For
.BR remove :
skip the y/n confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen without making any changes.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase terminal output detail.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress terminal output; write to log file only. Applied automatically
when stdout is not a terminal (e.g. cron, unattended-upgrades) unless
.B \-v
or
.B \-t
is explicitly set.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-terse
Minimal output for apt hooks. No banner, plain text with "apt-oob:" prefix.
Warnings print in yellow, errors in red. Overrides auto-quiet when set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt\-oob.conf
Global configuration file. Shell-sourceable key=value format.
Sourced at startup before paths are derived. Created by
.B oob init
with commented-out defaults if it does not exist.
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/
Default root directory for all apt-oob files. Overridable via
.B OOB_BASE
in
.IR /etc/apt\-oob.conf .
.TP
.B BANNER
Startup banner style. Set in
.IR /etc/apt\-oob.conf .
Values:
.BR fancy " (default) \(em DOS-style shaded box,"
.BR simple " \(em single line,"
.BR none " \(em no banner."
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/conf.d/
Package configuration files. Sourced in lexical order; numeric prefixes
.RI ( 10\- ", " 20\- )
control precedence. Each file configures one package.
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/checkver/
Version check scripts. Must print a single version string to stdout
and exit 0 on success.
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/dload/
Download URL resolution scripts. Receive version as $1, print URL to stdout.
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/checksum/
Checksum scripts. Receive version as $1, print
.I algo:hash
to stdout (e.g.
.IR sha256:abc123... ).
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/keys/
GPG public key files used for signature verification. Referenced by
.B GPG_KEY
in conf.d files.
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/live/
Extracted package installations.
.TP
.I /usr/local/apt\-oob/state/
Installed package state files. One file per package.
.TP
.I /var/log/apt\-oob.log
Log file. Syslog-style format. Overridable via
.B LOG_FILE
in
.IR /etc/apt\-oob.conf .
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99\-apt\-oob
APT hook file. Contains two hooks:
.B APT::Update::Post\-Invoke\-Success
runs
.B oob update
after
.BR "apt update" ;
.B DPkg::Post\-Invoke
runs
.B oob upgrade
after
.BR "apt upgrade" " or " "apt full\-upgrade" .
Written by
.BR "oob init" ,
removed by
.BR "oob deinit" .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Package configuration files under
.I conf.d/
are shell-sourceable key=value files.
.SS Built-in Variables
Available in conf.d files, expanded at source time:
.TP
.B ${OOB_BASE}
Root directory (default: /usr/local/apt-oob)
.TP
.B ${OOB_CONF}
Package configuration directory
.TP
.B ${OOB_CHECKVER}
Version check scripts directory
.TP
.B ${OOB_DLOAD}
Download scripts directory
.TP
.B ${OOB_CHECKSUM}
Checksum scripts directory
.TP
.B ${OOB_KEYS}
GPG keys directory
.TP
.B ${OOB_LIVE}
Installed packages directory
.TP
.B ${OOB_STATE}
State files directory
.TP
.B ${NAME}
Current package name (available after NAME= is defined in the conf file)
.SS Template Variables
Substituted at runtime using the version string from VERSION_CHECK. Available in DOWNLOAD, GPG_SIG_URL, and SYMLINKS:
.TP
.B %VERSION%
Full version string (e.g. 1.21.6)
.TP
.B %MAJOR%
Major component (e.g. 1)
.TP
.B %MINOR%
Minor component (e.g. 21)
.TP
.B %REVISION%
Revision component (e.g. 6)
.SS Fields
.TP
.B NAME
Package name. Used for directory naming under live/ and state/.
.TP
.B DOWNLOAD
Download source. Either an https:// URL supporting template variables
.RI ( %VERSION% ", " %MAJOR% ", " %MINOR% ", " %REVISION% )
or a script name resolved under dload/.
.TP
.B CHECKSUM
Either
.I none
to skip checksum verification, or a script name under checksum/.
If omitted entirely, a warning is logged and verification is skipped.
.TP
.B GPG_KEY
GPG public key filename under keys/. If set, oob imports the key into a
temporary keyring and verifies the detached signature (from GPG_SIG_URL)
against the downloaded archive. If not set, GPG verification is skipped.
If both CHECKSUM and GPG_KEY are set, both must pass.
.TP
.B GPG_SIG_URL
URL to fetch the detached GPG signature file. Supports template variables.
Required when GPG_KEY is set.
.TP
.B VERSION_CHECK
Version check script name under checkver/.
.TP
.B INSTALL_DIR
Base directory to extract the archive into. Typically
.IR ${OOB_LIVE}/${NAME} .
.TP
.B SYMLINKS
Pipe-separated list of symlinks in
.I linkname:relative_path
format. Pipe delimiter allows paths with spaces. Supports %VERSION% template
variables in relative paths. Optional; omit if no symlinks needed.
.TP
.B SYMLINK_DIR
Directory in which symlinks are created. Required if SYMLINKS is set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B oob
exits 0 on success. Per-package failures during
.B install
are handled internally and do not cause a non-zero exit unless a fatal
error occurs. This avoids false post-invoke failures reported by apt.
.PP
Before acting on a package,
.B oob
verifies that the state file and install directory agree. If the state
file exists but the install directory is missing (stale state), the state
is removed and the package is treated as not installed. If the install
directory exists but no state file is found (orphaned install), a warning
is printed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Upgrade all enabled packages:
.PP
.RS
.B oob upgrade
.RE
.PP
Check for updates without installing:
.PP
.RS
.B oob update
.RE
.PP
Install a single package:
.PP
.RS
.B oob install golang
.RE
.PP
Force reinstall a single package:
.PP
.RS
.B oob install golang \-f
.RE
.PP
Remove a package (also disables it):
.PP
.RS
.B oob remove firefox
.RE
.PP
Disable a package without removing it:
.PP
.RS
.B oob disable corretto
.RE
.PP
Re-enable a disabled package:
.PP
.RS
.B oob enable corretto
.RE
.PP
Set up the apt hook:
.PP
.RS
.B oob init
.RE
.SH INSTALLATION
Run
.B sudo ./install.sh
from the repository root. This executes
.B oob init
(creates directories, copies binary, writes config and apt hook), then
copies all package configs and scripts from the repo into
.IR /usr/local/apt\-oob/ .
It also symlinks
.B oob
into PATH.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt\-get (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
apt-oob contributors.
